  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>1. trans-&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CoCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math><br />or</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>trans</mo></math>-&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi>&#8467;</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d1feef5c-fa49-4551-8edd-72bc780f2cab-image.png\" style=\"width: 243px; height: 391px;\" /></p><p>As we know that ethylene diamine is a bidentate ligand and ammonia is a mono dentate ligand.</p><p>It means overall two ethylene diamine is required to replace the all neutral ligands (four ammonia) from the coordination sphere of this complex.</p>",
